This product bundles the third-party software listed below, each under its own
terms. Section 4 of the Apache License asks a distribution to carry the licence
and the copyright notices of what it redistributes; this file and the About
screen in the app are the two places it does.

Both are generated from, or held against, config/attribution/dependencies.txt,
which the build's checkAttribution task holds against gradle/libs.versions.toml.
The list covers every dependency the version catalogue declares that reaches a
distribution, plus the runtimes underneath them that the app could not run
without and that the catalogue never names - the Kotlin standard library,
SQLite, OkHttp, Bouncy Castle and Skia.

A year appears in a copyright line only where the dependency's own NOTICE states
one. Inventing the rest would have made this file look more precise and be less
true.

